WEBVTT

00:12.012 --> 00:14.681
HYEONJUNG ELEMENTARY SCHOOL
YEAR 1, CLASS 3

00:30.196 --> 00:31.489
YOON SE-A

00:31.573 --> 00:32.949
KIM U-JIN

00:33.033 --> 00:34.909
WE DO NOT CLIMB ON THE WINDOWS!

00:41.833 --> 00:44.669
OUR DREAMS

00:52.052 --> 00:54.804
OUR AMAZING HAND TREE

01:12.739 --> 01:17.744
HOME OF THE HEART

01:19.913 --> 01:20.830
Mom,

01:22.248 --> 01:23.583
I'm so sorry.

01:25.960 --> 01:27.378
I want to live.

01:29.422 --> 01:31.591
But living has become unbearable.

01:34.385 --> 01:37.055
If you read my diary, you'll understand.

01:41.226 --> 01:42.769
Mom, whatever you do,

01:44.062 --> 01:46.022
don't forgive the person
who did this to me

02:24.894 --> 02:26.312
Hello. Are you Choi Ji-seon?

02:27.438 --> 02:29.274
I see you haven't received the news.

02:29.357 --> 02:33.736
Today, we're carrying out psychological
evaluation for elementary school teachers.

02:33.820 --> 02:36.698
Your appointment's for now.
Will you follow me, please?

02:45.915 --> 02:48.001
I really like
what you've done with the room.

02:51.588 --> 02:52.547
Thanks.

03:16.154 --> 03:17.447
Today's mental health assessment

03:17.530 --> 03:20.200
is being conducted
in elementary schools nationwide.

03:20.283 --> 03:23.286
There will be no negative consequences
based on the results of the test,

03:23.369 --> 03:26.706
so you are encouraged
to answer as honestly as possible.

03:28.082 --> 03:30.126
3. I'M DOING RELATIVELY WELL
NOT AT ALL

03:33.463 --> 03:35.590
Did you check out
the TCM clinic I mentioned?

03:37.175 --> 03:38.051
Sorry?

03:39.135 --> 03:40.428
For your skin condition?

03:41.179 --> 03:42.931
It seems to be getting worse.

03:45.225 --> 03:48.436
Excuse me, Miss Choi.
Based on the results of your assessment,

03:48.519 --> 03:51.481
I wish to inform you that you have
been placed on administrative leave.

03:52.732 --> 03:54.984
You said there'd be
no negative consequences.

03:55.068 --> 03:57.779
Elementary school teachers everywhere
are stressed out.

03:57.862 --> 04:00.198
All across the country,
we are burned out and depressed.

04:00.281 --> 04:04.118
What you're doing is telling her
to give up on being a teacher.

04:04.202 --> 04:05.328
Don't you think

04:05.411 --> 04:07.413
that it's preferable to dying?

04:15.338 --> 04:16.881
In accordance with the psych results

04:16.965 --> 04:19.384
and the orders of
the Educational Rights Protection Bureau,

04:20.885 --> 04:23.054
you must take a leave of absence.

04:29.352 --> 04:31.813
LET'S BECOME A GOOD TEACHER!

04:34.232 --> 04:35.858
TOMORROW I'LL MEET THE CHILDREN

04:35.942 --> 04:38.987
Sir, my daughter
is an elementary school teacher.

04:39.612 --> 04:41.531
I'm afraid something's wrong at work.

04:41.614 --> 04:45.368
I found things in her diary
that I'm very worried about.

04:46.202 --> 04:50.581
Sir, please,
do what you can to help my daughter.

04:57.046 --> 05:01.134
WILL IT END IF I DIE?

05:01.217 --> 05:04.971
TEACH YOU A LESSON

05:06.097 --> 05:08.349
HYEONJUNG ELEMENTARY SCHOOL

05:08.433 --> 05:12.020
Can you tell me
what's gonna happen to me now?

05:12.103 --> 05:15.940
-First, you need to see a doctor.
-Miss. Your mother.

05:16.441 --> 05:18.401
She brought us
some of your personal belongings.

05:18.484 --> 05:20.194
She figured you'd need them.

05:20.278 --> 05:23.114
You're saying my mom knows about this?

05:23.698 --> 05:26.784
Your mother is the one
who brought your case to our attention.

05:27.785 --> 05:31.748
Seeing the doctor and receiving treatment
is the best thing you can do for her.

05:31.831 --> 05:33.082
Shall we go?

05:35.126 --> 05:39.505
Miss, do you know who's gonna
take care of the children in my class?

05:39.589 --> 05:42.091
Don't worry. A new homeroom teacher
is on the way.

05:42.175 --> 05:44.635
No. Don't do it!
That teacher will end up like me.

05:44.719 --> 05:47.472
No! There's no need to worry about that.

05:47.555 --> 05:49.849
Uh, this new teacher is

05:50.350 --> 05:52.602
a real piece of work.

06:06.574 --> 06:08.242
NA HWA-JIN

06:08.326 --> 06:11.079
All right, kids.
Why don't you all sit down, okay?

06:11.162 --> 06:12.830
Quiet down.

06:12.914 --> 06:15.375
Careful! Watch out! It's time to sit down.

06:16.793 --> 06:17.919
I said quiet!

06:22.340 --> 06:23.591
Quiet!

06:29.347 --> 06:31.265
Teacher!

06:32.392 --> 06:36.229
If you were in a fight with
our tae kwon do master, who would win?

06:36.312 --> 06:38.272
Sir, do you think you can beat Naruto?

06:38.356 --> 06:40.483
Excuse me, sir,
I need to use the bathroom.

06:40.566 --> 06:42.902
-This is not time for a bathroom break.
-I need to go, sir!

06:42.985 --> 06:45.655
-Just wait a minute. I said hold on.
-I need to pee! Sir, please!

06:45.738 --> 06:48.616
Hey, kid, what are you doing?
No! Not here! Just hang on!

06:56.791 --> 06:59.961
I gotta go too! I gotta use the bathroom.

07:05.758 --> 07:08.678
Me too! Me too! My turn! Me too!

07:09.720 --> 07:11.347
Faster, faster!

07:12.181 --> 07:14.559
Quick! Faster. I gotta go!

07:15.852 --> 07:18.688
Here's some nice omelet.
Lots of good protein. Who wants some?

07:18.771 --> 07:20.314
-I want egg!
-Me too!

07:20.398 --> 07:22.108
Nobody wants to eat their tomatoes?

07:26.779 --> 07:27.738
Teacher!

07:28.531 --> 07:30.032
-Hm?
-Can you make me a frog?

07:30.116 --> 07:32.952
This isn't the moment to be making frogs.
Do what you're told.

07:33.453 --> 07:35.163
Please, sir, make me a frog.

07:35.246 --> 07:38.040
This isn't the time for origami!
Just do as I said.

07:43.629 --> 07:45.339
Don't cry. I wasn't angry with you.

07:45.840 --> 07:47.758
So you flip this side over again.

07:49.385 --> 07:52.972
And then you fold like this,
and like this.

07:53.639 --> 07:55.057
Then you fold the back legs.

07:55.141 --> 07:57.894
Yeon-Seo, have you ever eaten
frogs' legs for dinner?

07:57.977 --> 08:01.814
-Yuck! Do people really eat frogs' legs?
-Well, I've tasted them.

08:01.898 --> 08:04.525
-Huh.
-There you go. One pretty frog!

08:04.609 --> 08:06.569
Hop! Whoa!

08:29.258 --> 08:30.301
Ga-yun,

08:30.801 --> 08:33.054
was teaching always this hard?

08:37.725 --> 08:40.478
Those damn frogs, they killed me!

08:52.281 --> 08:53.908
LET'S BECOME A GOOD TEACHER!

08:53.991 --> 08:55.576
Today, we're gonna learn

08:55.660 --> 08:58.162
about the ways
to express our feelings with words.

08:58.246 --> 09:02.166
For example, what do you say
when you're feeling really happy?

09:03.709 --> 09:07.338
Very good. "I'm happy
and I'm in a really good mood."

09:07.964 --> 09:10.967
It's important that we learn
to express our feelings with words.

09:11.050 --> 09:15.263
So, children, when we are in class, I hope
you will always tell me how you feel.

09:15.346 --> 09:16.264
Okay?

09:16.347 --> 09:19.267
I'm so happy to be here.
Let me tell you my name.

09:24.105 --> 09:26.524
CHOI JI-SEON

09:31.487 --> 09:34.740
Hello, everyone!
It's so nice to meet you all.

09:34.824 --> 09:37.785
My name is Miss Choi Ji-seon.

09:40.580 --> 09:44.083
I hope we will all get along together.
You all know who I am now.

09:44.709 --> 09:48.129
So, maybe you would like
to introduce yourselves to me?

09:48.212 --> 09:49.672
Yeah!

09:50.256 --> 09:51.215
So, how about you?

09:53.175 --> 09:54.802
My name is Kim Yong-hun.

09:57.346 --> 09:58.556
My name is Lee Yeon-seo.

10:14.030 --> 10:15.239
You're Kim U-jin, right?

10:15.823 --> 10:17.366
It's all right, U-jin. You can sit down.

10:18.659 --> 10:19.744
A round of applause.

10:23.039 --> 10:24.707
-Goodbye.
-Bye, Miss.

10:24.790 --> 10:27.376
Bye-bye, children. See you tomorrow.

10:27.460 --> 10:30.087
Hello, U-jin's mom.
U-jin, see you tomorrow!

10:30.171 --> 10:32.423
-Say goodbye to your teacher.
-See you tomorrow.

10:32.506 --> 10:34.425
Miss Choi, please take good care
of my U-jin.

10:34.508 --> 10:36.802
Of course, ma'am.
Thank you for trusting me.

10:37.428 --> 10:39.972
If it's all right with you,
may I contact you from time to time

10:40.056 --> 10:41.641
if I have any questions or concerns?

10:41.724 --> 10:42.933
Of course, ma'am.

10:43.017 --> 10:46.937
You may contact me by using the Talk Mate
app. Feel free to leave your message.

10:47.021 --> 10:50.191
Work hours are between 8 a.m. and 6 p.m.

10:50.274 --> 10:52.193
You live in the Stern Apartments, right?

10:53.110 --> 10:54.487
Oh. Yes.

10:54.570 --> 10:55.821
Come on.

10:55.905 --> 10:56.989
Well done today.

10:57.531 --> 10:59.742
-Shall we go?
-Did you bring your jacket?

11:01.202 --> 11:02.578
Did you remember your lunchbox?

11:09.377 --> 11:12.880
This is U-jin's mom. I'm just
a little concerned about something.

11:13.631 --> 11:17.677
Earlier, when you told U-jin to sit,
your tone was much too harsh.

11:18.219 --> 11:21.764
I'm just concerned that he might think
that you don't like him.

11:22.431 --> 11:24.892
I'll do my best
to make sure he doesn't feel that way.

11:30.189 --> 11:32.483
I think
it will be bad for his self-esteem.

11:32.566 --> 11:33.859
You understand, right?

11:33.943 --> 11:35.444
Of course.

11:36.028 --> 11:39.865
Kim U-jin. Request to make sure
not to negatively impact his self-esteem.

11:43.285 --> 11:44.120
Hm.

11:50.835 --> 11:54.088
You're not sure, is that it?
You want me to explain it again?

11:55.339 --> 11:57.383
Miss, I know the answer. I can do it!

11:57.466 --> 12:00.511
Me too!

12:00.594 --> 12:02.263
Quiet please.

12:06.934 --> 12:07.768
It's okay.

12:13.190 --> 12:14.608
U-jin's feeling down.

12:14.692 --> 12:18.112
In the future, don't make him
solve math problems in front of the class.

12:20.448 --> 12:22.658
About the incorrect answers
on U-jin's spelling report.

12:22.742 --> 12:26.495
Mark them with something other than
a slash. It's bad for his self-confidence.

12:28.581 --> 12:29.749
"Don't do that. No. Stop."

12:29.832 --> 12:32.877
Please refrain from using
words of restraint such as these.

12:34.837 --> 12:38.466
When he clashes with one of the other
kids, take my child's side no matter what.

12:38.549 --> 12:42.470
Avoid using words that imply commands
or orders. Make suggestions or requests.

12:42.553 --> 12:45.139
Do not force him to greet people
with the traditional bowed head.

12:45.222 --> 12:48.893
Feeling obliged and pressured to bow
to people is bad for his self-esteem.

12:48.976 --> 12:52.062
Do not scold children
for being too loud in the classroom.

12:52.146 --> 12:53.814
It crushes their spirit.

13:02.865 --> 13:04.325
You can't catch me!

13:06.994 --> 13:08.621
Ha! You missed me!

13:10.498 --> 13:13.417
-Miss, here! Look at this!
-So cool!

13:18.172 --> 13:20.549
You're overreacting. Seriously.

13:20.633 --> 13:21.884
-Ji-seon!
-How come you're late?

13:21.967 --> 13:23.302
I told you she'd make it.

13:23.385 --> 13:24.970
I've missed my bestie.

13:25.054 --> 13:26.305
Ji-seon!

13:29.642 --> 13:31.852
No way! What date is it?

13:31.936 --> 13:33.938
-It's in the invitation.
-Sorry, one moment.

13:34.021 --> 13:35.105
Where's the venue?

13:35.606 --> 13:37.107
Wear bras without straps.

13:37.191 --> 13:39.902
It may distract the boys
and it's inappropriate.

13:39.985 --> 13:43.030
-A toast to Won-ho!
-Ji-seon, come on, relax.

13:43.113 --> 13:44.782
-Cheers!
-Cheers!

13:57.336 --> 13:59.505
LONG TIME NO GET-TOGETHER

14:00.089 --> 14:01.966
Aren't you ashamed of posting this?

14:02.049 --> 14:03.467
What if the children see this?

14:03.551 --> 14:06.637
You're exposing them
to unnecessary sexualized content.

14:11.725 --> 14:13.769
How did she find my Instagram account?

14:13.853 --> 14:16.730
It seems like
you spend all your time partying.

14:16.814 --> 14:18.649
You realize it's my taxes
that pays your salary.

14:18.732 --> 14:21.193
Spend more of your time
prepping your class.

14:21.277 --> 14:24.488
I wouldn't mind
if her comments concerned the children.

14:24.572 --> 14:28.117
But she's crossed the line. We're talking
about my private and personal life.

14:28.784 --> 14:30.327
Change your Instagram account.

14:31.120 --> 14:33.539
Better still, stop using social media.

14:33.622 --> 14:35.791
Why should I?
I haven't done anything wrong.

14:35.875 --> 14:38.711
I tried to fight them on it.
I even pressed charges.

14:38.794 --> 14:40.754
Then the parents signed a petition.

14:40.838 --> 14:43.048
Really. I tried my best to talk with them.

14:43.549 --> 14:46.510
They complained that I always
sided with the teachers.

14:46.594 --> 14:48.888
They didn't even listen to a thing I said.

14:48.971 --> 14:51.265
No matter what I did, they shut me down.

14:51.348 --> 14:55.269
And in the end, everyone suffered.
The entire school body did.

15:02.026 --> 15:03.777
REMOVE "INSTAGRAM"?
DELETE APP

15:04.278 --> 15:05.696
DELETE "INSTAGRAM"?
DELETE

15:12.202 --> 15:15.748
I suppose I can
go back on Instagram after I retire.

15:15.831 --> 15:18.500
I need to consider the children.

16:15.933 --> 16:18.227
HOME OF THE HEART

16:52.928 --> 16:53.762
U-jin?

16:55.472 --> 16:56.473
You like this?

16:56.557 --> 16:58.350
I call it the Home of the Heart.

16:58.434 --> 17:00.728
Here, you can play
and have fun with all your friends.

17:06.316 --> 17:08.527
How are you feeling today, U-jin?

17:08.610 --> 17:10.446
What would you like
to do with your friends?

17:12.031 --> 17:14.283
I like to have fun and play with them.

17:14.366 --> 17:17.327
That sounds great.
This is your Home of the Heart.

17:17.411 --> 17:19.997
Here, you are allowed
to express all your feelings.

17:20.080 --> 17:21.331
So why not

17:21.874 --> 17:23.834
do what your feelings tell you to do?

17:28.255 --> 17:29.798
Okay. My turn now.

17:32.885 --> 17:34.636
Yeah!

17:42.352 --> 17:44.646
Whoo! Careful, everyone. Watch out.

17:44.730 --> 17:46.523
-U-jin, you're so good!
-Whoa!

17:49.109 --> 17:51.070
-Bravo, U-jin!
-Yeah!

17:51.862 --> 17:53.489
Over here! Pass!

17:53.572 --> 17:55.824
That's it, Eun-ho! Well done. Very good.

17:55.908 --> 17:59.244
-Pass, pass!
-Hey, over here! Pass the ball!

18:04.208 --> 18:05.709
U-jin. I'm really sorry.

18:05.793 --> 18:06.877
I got it!

18:06.960 --> 18:08.879
-Ow!
-Stop, U-jin!

18:08.962 --> 18:13.092
"Don't do that. No! Stop."
Refrain from using words of restraint.

18:13.175 --> 18:14.968
When he clashes
with one of the other kids,

18:15.052 --> 18:16.804
take my child's side no matter what.

18:17.971 --> 18:20.933
Ow! U-jin, stop. That hurts!

18:21.016 --> 18:22.851
U-jin!

18:24.144 --> 18:28.857
I want my mommy!

18:28.941 --> 18:31.193
Mommy!

18:31.777 --> 18:34.154
-It hurts. My eye hurts!
-Seo-jun, you okay?

18:34.238 --> 18:35.572
Mommy!

18:39.159 --> 18:41.453
Hello. Thank you for coming.

18:42.079 --> 18:46.166
I'm sure you must be feeling
a little shocked. Please, have some tea.

18:54.758 --> 18:58.387
I spoke with Seo-jun.
He told me his version of what happened.

18:59.304 --> 19:02.432
Boys will be boys, and when
they play sports, these things can happen.

19:03.976 --> 19:06.478
And sometimes, they fight.
I understand that.

19:06.562 --> 19:08.981
Thank you for being so understanding.

19:09.064 --> 19:11.316
The children have apologized and made up.

19:13.152 --> 19:15.279
Are you saying you made U-jin apologize?

19:21.076 --> 19:23.745
U-jin was at fault,
so of course he had to apologize.

19:23.829 --> 19:27.541
My son told me that Seo-jun pushed him
first. He started the whole thing.

19:28.458 --> 19:30.419
So he's the one who should apologize.

19:32.796 --> 19:34.131
Excuse me.

19:34.840 --> 19:36.633
My son's been seriously injured.

19:36.717 --> 19:38.385
He could have lost an eye.

19:38.468 --> 19:40.596
My son has also been injured.

19:40.679 --> 19:43.182
Imagine how hurt he must have been
to be crying.

19:43.682 --> 19:46.143
That's an interesting thing to focus on.

19:46.226 --> 19:49.021
We are trying to move past this
for the children's sake.

19:49.104 --> 19:51.398
Your son hurt my U-jin's feelings!

19:51.481 --> 19:53.233
If he is traumatized by this,

19:53.734 --> 19:56.904
it's your fault,
and I'll make sure your son pays for it.

19:56.987 --> 19:58.989
-What?
-Ladies, please.

19:59.072 --> 20:01.116
I'm begging you. Please calm down.

20:01.200 --> 20:03.660
Miss Choi, as their teacher,
why aren't you speaking up?

20:03.744 --> 20:06.830
We all know that U-jin is a loner and
doesn't get on with the other children.

20:06.914 --> 20:09.124
Now I've met you,
I understand why that is.

20:09.208 --> 20:10.792
-Watch it!
-Try me!

20:10.876 --> 20:13.629
Call a meeting then.
You won't be so full of it then.

20:13.712 --> 20:15.631
-All right! Bring it on.
-Sit down.

20:15.714 --> 20:17.090
Call a meeting. I'm game.

20:17.174 --> 20:19.384
Please, ladies, calm down.
I'm begging you.

20:19.468 --> 20:21.303
You need to calm down. Please.

20:22.012 --> 20:25.432
Mrs. Lee, I have the feeling
that a school violence committee meeting

20:25.515 --> 20:27.017
would be unfavorable for U-jin.

20:27.100 --> 20:30.812
-Why don't we all just apologize--
-You do realize all of this is your fault?

20:32.314 --> 20:35.692
I told you to always take U-jin's side
if there were fights at school.

20:35.776 --> 20:37.194
And you told me you were on board.

20:37.277 --> 20:39.863
Ma'am, I never said
that I agreed with that.

20:41.448 --> 20:42.449
What did you say?

20:43.617 --> 20:47.371
Why are you suddenly changing your mind
instead of speaking up back then?

20:47.871 --> 20:49.873
I will speak with Seo-jun's mother--

20:49.957 --> 20:51.959
What will you say
at the violence committee meeting?

20:54.753 --> 20:55.963
Well…

20:57.381 --> 20:59.758
-I have to tell them exactly what I saw.
-Yes, and?

21:00.759 --> 21:02.427
What exactly did you see?

21:09.393 --> 21:10.602
Give me your phone number.

21:10.686 --> 21:14.022
It's against school policy to give out
our personal numbers. We use Talk Mate.

21:14.106 --> 21:16.358
Are you saying I can't reach you
after work hours?

21:16.441 --> 21:20.362
You wanna go and enjoy your life
after what you've done to my son?

21:20.445 --> 21:22.948
-No, ma'am. I didn't say that--
-Give it to me!

21:31.206 --> 21:33.166
All of this is your fault, Miss Choi.

21:34.209 --> 21:35.544
You do realize that?

21:36.044 --> 21:38.588
And right now, my husband is really angry.

21:39.089 --> 21:40.507
Maybe I should call him.

21:41.341 --> 21:44.386
-Yeah?
-I'm sorry, ma'am.

21:45.387 --> 21:48.432
A homeroom teacher
isn't qualified to help you with that.

22:05.490 --> 22:07.743
-Hello. Good morning.
-This is U-jin's mother.

22:08.618 --> 22:09.786
Mrs. Lee.

22:10.329 --> 22:12.289
How did you find my private number?

22:12.372 --> 22:15.834
That's hardly important now.
What are you gonna say to the committee?

22:17.961 --> 22:20.380
-Miss Choi, answer me.
-I have to…

22:20.464 --> 22:22.090
U-JIN'S MOTHER

22:31.933 --> 22:34.269
Hello? Miss Choi!

22:34.353 --> 22:35.604
Yes, ma'am?

22:35.687 --> 22:37.647
Why did you take so long to answer?

22:39.066 --> 22:41.401
-Hello? Are you there?
-Uh… Uh…

22:41.485 --> 22:43.653
My apologies, ma'am.

22:47.574 --> 22:51.078
Did you get my messages?
Why aren't you answering me?!

22:51.161 --> 22:54.081
It's just that I'm in the middle
of prepping the class.

22:55.457 --> 22:56.625
U-JIN'S MOTHER

22:59.628 --> 23:00.921
U-JIN'S MOTHER

23:06.426 --> 23:08.637
U-JIN'S MOTHER

23:10.722 --> 23:11.973
U-JIN'S MOTHER

23:13.934 --> 23:17.312
I told you to take U-jin's side
if there were fights at school.

23:17.396 --> 23:18.897
And you told me you were on board.

23:18.980 --> 23:22.609
You want to go and enjoy your life
after what you've done to my son?

23:25.195 --> 23:27.489
You do realize
all this is your fault, right?

23:28.365 --> 23:30.158
And you told me you were on board.

23:30.242 --> 23:31.993
Miss Choi!

23:33.078 --> 23:34.121
Miss Choi!

23:39.668 --> 23:41.503
All of this is your fault, Miss Choi.

23:41.586 --> 23:45.549
All of this is your fault, Miss Choi.
All of this is your fault, Miss Choi.

23:45.632 --> 23:47.884
Miss Choi! Miss Choi!

24:05.193 --> 24:08.613
Hello, Miss Choi.
Why aren't you answering your phone?

24:09.114 --> 24:13.410
Do you feel guilty, Miss? Is that it?
Come down. Let's talk face to face, okay?

24:13.493 --> 24:14.411
Who is it?

24:17.789 --> 24:19.791
I'm just going out for a moment.

24:19.875 --> 24:20.876
Where to?

24:22.919 --> 24:24.296
Where are you going?

24:25.088 --> 24:27.716
That makes no sense.
U-jin was not the cause of it!

24:28.383 --> 24:31.887
It's unacceptable.
Why would the committee rule against us?

24:31.970 --> 24:34.097
There's nothing to worry about.

24:34.181 --> 24:36.516
All you need to do
is submit a written apology.

24:36.600 --> 24:38.685
-It was you, wasn't it?
-Sorry?

24:38.768 --> 24:40.479
You took their side.

24:41.771 --> 24:43.815
You're mistaken, ma'am.
I didn't take sides.

24:43.899 --> 24:45.984
Just because I was a little critical
about your work,

24:46.067 --> 24:48.320
you bullied my son just to get back at me.

24:52.324 --> 24:56.077
You don't deserve to be a school teacher.

24:56.995 --> 24:59.789
I can't trust you with my son,
so you should quit.

24:59.873 --> 25:02.167
And my husband is very angry with you.

25:02.250 --> 25:04.419
I advise you to watch out.

25:37.702 --> 25:38.537
Papa?

25:50.173 --> 25:51.383
U-jin, come with me.

25:53.843 --> 25:55.136
Come on, let's go.

25:59.474 --> 26:00.517
I said let's go!

26:01.351 --> 26:03.770
Mr. Kim, right now
we're in the middle of class.

26:03.853 --> 26:04.938
What the hell?

26:08.817 --> 26:11.403
Sir, please stop it. Think about U-jin.

26:16.700 --> 26:18.326
What the…

26:18.827 --> 26:20.912
Who the hell do you think you are?

26:23.498 --> 26:24.332
Let's go.

26:25.500 --> 26:26.668
Out of my way.

26:33.258 --> 26:34.509
Don't worry, children.

26:37.012 --> 26:38.972
It's all right, Ji-yeong. Don't cry.

26:45.353 --> 26:49.274
TEACHERS' RIGHTS PROTECTION COMMITTEE
NOTICE TO ATTEND

26:53.445 --> 26:54.904
VICTIMIZED TEACHER: CHOI JI-SEON

26:54.988 --> 26:56.781
Do whatever you want. I don't care.

26:56.865 --> 27:00.201
Even if what I did is against the rules,
I'll just apologize later.

27:00.702 --> 27:02.454
Go ahead and call the ERPB.

27:04.998 --> 27:08.126
Did you think I'd just sit back
and watch a teacher abuse her power?

27:12.547 --> 27:14.549
I filed a complaint against you.

27:17.761 --> 27:20.430
You picked on U-jin,
and humiliated him in front of the class.

27:20.513 --> 27:24.351
When I raised the question with you, you
encouraged another child to ignore him.

27:24.893 --> 27:27.187
You lured my son
into that Home of the Heart thing,

27:27.270 --> 27:28.938
and that's where
you emotionally abused him.

27:29.022 --> 27:31.149
But, ma'am, none of this is true.

27:31.232 --> 27:33.610
We'll see about that.
The police will investigate anyway.

27:33.693 --> 27:36.446
I would never humiliate
or emotionally abuse U-jin.

27:37.989 --> 27:41.660
Are you saying I imagined it all?
That I'm doing this to get back at you?

27:42.827 --> 27:44.788
And his behavior, how do you explain that?

27:45.622 --> 27:49.250
You say you've done nothing wrong,
yet my son spends his time crying at home.

27:49.334 --> 27:53.171
I feel very sorry for U-jin, ma'am,
but you have no right to do this.

27:53.254 --> 27:57.717
No right?! U-jin's been wronged, but his
teacher won't take responsibility for it.

27:57.801 --> 27:59.469
Do you want me to resign? Is that it?

27:59.969 --> 28:01.346
I went to see a lawyer too.

28:02.263 --> 28:03.682
The law has been changed.

28:03.765 --> 28:06.643
So even if you accuse me
of child abuse, I…

28:06.726 --> 28:09.020
I won't be suspended immediately
like before.

28:09.521 --> 28:10.855
I don't really care.

28:11.356 --> 28:12.482
Go and teach.

28:12.565 --> 28:14.818
And when your day is done,
head to the police station

28:14.901 --> 28:17.153
where you can help the investigation.

28:17.237 --> 28:20.448
The whole process can be very long.
Maybe more than a year.

28:20.532 --> 28:22.450
If you can't handle it,
you should quit teaching.

28:29.624 --> 28:32.419
And when they find me innocent,
what will you do then?

28:37.090 --> 28:39.092
Well, of course, I'll apologize.

28:39.718 --> 28:40.844
That's all I can do.

28:41.344 --> 28:42.721
Because that's the law.

29:19.132 --> 29:20.300
Ji-seon.

29:20.383 --> 29:23.052
I saw this on a parents' forum.
Have you seen it?

29:23.553 --> 29:25.388
This looks really serious.

29:26.848 --> 29:29.642
1-3 HOMEROOM TEACHER
AT HYEONJUNG ELEMENTARY IS A CHILD ABUSER

29:32.103 --> 29:33.605
LOOKS CAN BE DECEIVING
SO SHOCKING

29:35.732 --> 29:38.485
PLEASE SHARE THIS POST UNTIL THE DAY
CHOI JI-SEON IS PUNISHED

29:38.568 --> 29:39.611
MS. CHOI 010-0235-7462

29:51.122 --> 29:54.083
All right. First grade, Class 3.
Come on in, please.

29:55.543 --> 29:56.795
Okay, let's go.

30:02.967 --> 30:04.552
How about an orange?

30:11.351 --> 30:14.604
Would you like some more rice?
Is that enough? Enjoy your meal.

30:14.687 --> 30:15.772
Thank you.

30:15.855 --> 30:17.398
-Are you ready?
-Yeah.

30:17.482 --> 30:20.777
-Let's do it.
-Rock, paper, scissors, shoot!

30:21.694 --> 30:24.447
Parents keep calling
the school to complain.

30:24.948 --> 30:28.076
Some are even coming to see me
to discuss this in person.

30:28.576 --> 30:31.079
They're saying that if I allow you
to keep working here,

30:31.162 --> 30:33.873
they'll stop sending their children
to our school.

30:36.000 --> 30:37.168
I'm sorry.

30:37.669 --> 30:40.839
It's not fair to tell you
to hold on and to hang tight.

30:52.058 --> 30:59.065
HOME OF THE HEART

31:20.169 --> 31:22.171
TEACHER
KIM U-JIN

31:26.009 --> 31:28.219
KIDDOS IN YEAR 1, CLASS 3

31:28.303 --> 31:29.721
KIM U-JIN: THOUGHTFUL, SMILEY

31:29.804 --> 31:31.139
KIM YUN-U: VERY CONSIDERATE

31:36.519 --> 31:39.647
MS. CHOI, BE HAPPY

31:43.484 --> 31:47.155
It would have felt as though
she were standing alone in a dense forest.

31:47.238 --> 31:48.907
IT'S HARD TO OPEN MY EYES IN THE MORNING

31:48.990 --> 31:51.284
In a place where people
were watching her from all around,

31:51.367 --> 31:54.203
ready at any moment
to pounce on her and rip her to shreds.

31:55.872 --> 31:57.624
A woman all alone and defenseless.

31:57.707 --> 31:59.417
I'M MAKING MY OWN STUDENTS UNHAPPY

31:59.500 --> 32:00.418
WILL IT END IF I DIE?

32:00.501 --> 32:02.253
So why are the police investigating?

32:02.337 --> 32:04.839
She followed the curriculum
and the teaching protocols.

32:04.923 --> 32:08.009
Because once a report has been filed,
the police have to investigate.

32:08.092 --> 32:10.595
So these people can file a complaint
without any proof?

32:11.179 --> 32:12.138
They're the rules.

32:12.221 --> 32:13.348
Seriously?

32:13.431 --> 32:16.434
In this kind of case,
suspicion alone is all that's required.

32:18.686 --> 32:21.439
This data shows
that the number of teachers

32:21.522 --> 32:24.651
that have been reported for child abuse
over the past few years

32:24.734 --> 32:26.945
has increased to over 11,000.

32:27.445 --> 32:30.281
And yet only 1.6% of them

32:30.865 --> 32:32.075
end up being prosecuted.

32:33.076 --> 32:34.827
This means that most of these teachers

32:34.911 --> 32:37.747
have been subjected
to undue stress and anxiety

32:38.456 --> 32:40.583
even though they'd done nothing wrong.

32:41.709 --> 32:44.629
Even if the teacher is found not guilty,

32:44.712 --> 32:46.756
the person or parent
who has filed the report

32:46.839 --> 32:49.968
cannot be punished
for making false accusations by the judge.

32:50.468 --> 32:52.387
Many parents are taking advantage of that.

32:52.470 --> 32:53.846
Even if they're wrong

32:54.639 --> 32:56.933
and the teacher's innocent,
they just say, "My bad."

32:57.016 --> 32:58.142
You gotta be kidding!

32:58.226 --> 33:00.311
The problem is
the current wording of the law

33:00.395 --> 33:02.981
gives an ambiguous definition
of emotional abuse.

33:03.064 --> 33:05.149
These are invisible wounds.

33:06.275 --> 33:08.403
They have no choice
but to believe the parent.

33:08.486 --> 33:10.863
And it's very difficult
for teachers to prove otherwise.

33:10.947 --> 33:12.949
The teachers are exhausted and alone.

33:13.032 --> 33:15.284
Despite the fact
that most of them will be found innocent,

33:15.368 --> 33:17.996
until then, a full investigation
has to be done.

33:18.079 --> 33:20.415
And sometimes, the teachers
are removed from their class.

33:20.498 --> 33:23.126
The teachers are told not to hit children,
not even with a flower,

33:23.209 --> 33:25.545
but this is like handing
a loaded gun to the parents.

33:25.628 --> 33:29.257
How do we expect them to block the bullets
that are being fired at them?

33:30.008 --> 33:31.217
Unbelievable!

33:31.300 --> 33:36.764
Currently, it means that if a teacher
is reported to the school for child abuse,

33:36.848 --> 33:38.725
we've got no way to protect them.

33:43.771 --> 33:44.772
Well, then,

33:45.732 --> 33:47.025
we must be their shields.

33:47.734 --> 33:49.152
It's not going to be easy.

33:50.069 --> 33:53.573
To bring about change, it's one step
at a time. That's what we'll do.

33:54.824 --> 33:56.409
First step, Inspector Hwa-jin,

33:56.492 --> 34:00.413
you must manage those parents
who abuse the spirit of the law.

34:12.800 --> 34:14.677
I'm all fired up after that speech.

34:14.761 --> 34:16.054
Let's go!

34:16.137 --> 34:19.974
"You must manage those parents
who abuse the spirit of the law."

34:24.645 --> 34:25.730
Miss Choi Ji-seon?

34:26.230 --> 34:27.815
Come with me, please.

34:30.109 --> 34:31.194
COUNSELING ROOM

34:31.277 --> 34:32.236
Best of luck.

34:34.030 --> 34:37.492
Paging Dr. Han So-jin.
Please contact the front desk.

34:38.076 --> 34:41.329
Orderly is requested for Room 523
at the Acute Care Unit.

34:41.412 --> 34:42.914
Visiting hours are over at 5 p.m.

34:42.997 --> 34:46.667
I can't believe that someone would
harass another human being like that.

34:46.751 --> 34:48.503
I swear that people
are starting to scare me.

34:48.586 --> 34:53.382
I get that.
But reptilians are much, much scarier.

34:53.466 --> 34:54.759
-Rep what?
-Reptilians.

34:54.842 --> 34:57.595
Alien beings that have infiltrated Earth.

34:57.678 --> 34:59.889
Aliens don't exist, Bong.

34:59.972 --> 35:03.392
Actually, it's true. There's a lot
of evidence confirming that they exist.

35:03.476 --> 35:04.852
Do you really believe that stuff?

35:07.980 --> 35:11.859
Well, it's probably better
if we stop talking.

35:12.443 --> 35:16.155
Why? Is my conversation
boring to you, Bong?

35:16.239 --> 35:18.282
No. It's just that I have the impression

35:18.366 --> 35:22.453
that it's a waste of time speaking
with people who aren't open-minded.

35:22.954 --> 35:25.498
I understand. Deputy Director Bong?

35:25.998 --> 35:27.416
-Yes?
-These rep--

35:27.500 --> 35:31.379
-Reptilians.
-Yeah. The rep… whatever.

35:31.462 --> 35:32.839
Yeah?

35:33.422 --> 35:36.050
Well, how about I show you
something even scarier?

35:36.759 --> 35:37.718
Uh…

35:38.469 --> 35:41.681
Agh!

35:43.933 --> 35:48.437
Well, then, how about I show you how to
write the character for "patience" again?

35:48.938 --> 35:51.023
You start with the root for knife

35:51.107 --> 35:52.483
and the radical for heart.

35:52.567 --> 35:54.777
Then you slice the heart with the knife.

35:55.528 --> 35:57.196
Da-dum, da-dum.

36:20.136 --> 36:23.389
All right. So, would anyone
like to step up and solve this?

36:29.729 --> 36:31.063
Would U-jin like to give it a try?

36:31.147 --> 36:35.193
Oh!

36:35.276 --> 36:36.277
FRIDAY, MAY 8
DAILY REPORT

36:36.360 --> 36:38.905
Today in math class,
the children and I spent our time

36:38.988 --> 36:40.907
solving problems on the chalkboard.

36:41.407 --> 36:43.576
The children were very attentive.

36:43.659 --> 36:46.913
But if you think improvement is needed,
feel free to review at home.

36:59.800 --> 37:01.177
Whoa!

37:02.053 --> 37:04.305
Whoa! Are you all right, ma'am?

37:04.388 --> 37:06.515
Let me help you.

37:06.599 --> 37:08.434
Why were you hiding behind the door?

37:08.517 --> 37:10.436
Well, this is…

37:10.519 --> 37:13.064
Well, this is where I teach.
It's my classroom.

37:13.147 --> 37:14.523
The new homeroom teacher.

37:14.607 --> 37:18.569
Oh. So that means
that you're U-jin's new teacher?

37:18.653 --> 37:23.282
Ah, you must be his mom!
I'm pleased to meet you, ma'am.

37:23.366 --> 37:24.951
Welcome. My name is Na Hwa-jin.

37:25.034 --> 37:28.579
So, what brings you to school
so early in the morning, ma'am?

37:28.663 --> 37:31.499
Yesterday, you asked U-jin
to solve some problems, didn't you?

37:31.582 --> 37:33.876
Yes, and I was really impressed.

37:33.960 --> 37:35.503
U-jin is a really smart kid.

37:35.586 --> 37:38.130
I got the feeling
that he's been working very hard.

37:38.214 --> 37:42.051
And I'm guessing that you've been
studying a lot with him at home, right?

37:42.134 --> 37:43.678
Well, no. Not really.

37:43.761 --> 37:46.055
So that means he's just naturally gifted.

37:46.555 --> 37:48.474
By any chance, are you gifted too?

37:48.557 --> 37:51.686
I bet you did well in school
and U-jin takes after you. Am I right?

37:51.769 --> 37:54.230
-Well, it's true I was a good student.
-I knew it!

37:54.313 --> 37:59.151
If I may say so, you look like
a good student. You really do.

37:59.235 --> 38:01.070
Sir, from now on, however,

38:01.153 --> 38:03.281
would you please not ask U-jin
to the chalkboard?

38:03.364 --> 38:05.658
I'm afraid that it might
affect his self-confidence.

38:05.741 --> 38:08.077
Ah! Of course, yes.
I didn't even think of that.

38:08.160 --> 38:11.372
Thank you for enlightening me.
I appreciate it.

38:11.455 --> 38:14.625
I'm so happy that we understand each
other. Now I won't have to worry at all.

38:14.709 --> 38:16.877
I'm not sure I understand.
Worried about what?

38:16.961 --> 38:19.255
The previous teacher was a strange woman.

38:19.880 --> 38:22.174
I promise that I will never
become a strange teacher.

38:22.883 --> 38:24.552
Thanks.

38:27.638 --> 38:28.472
NA HWA-JIN

38:29.432 --> 38:30.933
Hello. What can I do for you?

38:31.017 --> 38:33.936
Well, you see, U-jin keeps falling asleep.

38:34.020 --> 38:37.273
-I was wondering what I should do?
-Go ahead and wake him up.

38:37.356 --> 38:39.650
Every student has the right to sleep
if they want,

38:39.734 --> 38:42.486
so I don't want to abuse his rights.

38:42.570 --> 38:44.405
That's okay.
You have my permission to do it.

38:44.488 --> 38:45.823
That's perfect. Thanks.

38:46.949 --> 38:48.951
Sorry to bother.
How should I wake him up, ma'am?

38:49.035 --> 38:50.328
Just give him a little shake.

38:50.411 --> 38:53.080
I'm afraid that physical contact
would get me accused of child abuse.

38:53.164 --> 38:55.416
Well, why not call him by his name then?

38:55.499 --> 38:56.709
Ah!

38:58.294 --> 38:59.837
If I speak his name too loudly

38:59.920 --> 39:02.798
it might startle him and it could be
emotionally stressful for him.

39:02.882 --> 39:04.717
Ask the student next to him
to wake him up.

39:04.800 --> 39:07.011
He might feel embarrassed,
and it would traumatize him.

39:07.094 --> 39:08.929
Then leave him alone and forget it.

39:09.013 --> 39:12.183
But, ma'am, um, that's neglect,
which means abuse.

39:14.602 --> 39:17.480
Hello? Mrs. Lee? Are you there?

39:21.525 --> 39:23.986
Oh, give me a break!

39:31.577 --> 39:32.578
Ma'am, it's me.

39:32.661 --> 39:35.081
I was just wondering
what I could use instead of a slash

39:35.164 --> 39:37.875
to indicate the incorrect answers
on U-jin's spelling test?

39:37.958 --> 39:41.087
You have lots of options.
You can use a star.

39:41.170 --> 39:44.173
Yeah, but stars are used
to mark something as important.

39:44.256 --> 39:45.299
A triangle?

39:45.383 --> 39:48.928
Ah, that's the symbol we use
when the answer is partially correct.

39:51.847 --> 39:53.682
Polygons? Semicircle?

39:55.267 --> 39:56.227
Okay.

39:58.104 --> 40:00.981
-Just use a slash.
-Understood. Thank you!

40:01.065 --> 40:02.817
-I'll call you later.
-Shit!

40:03.859 --> 40:05.820
Shit!

40:10.449 --> 40:11.992
I have a few questions.

40:12.076 --> 40:13.494
What are your thoughts about parents

40:13.577 --> 40:16.455
who contact teachers directly
on their personal phones?

40:16.539 --> 40:19.500
My understanding is that contacting
teachers on their personal phones

40:19.583 --> 40:22.253
is a violation of their rights
and their right to privacy.

40:22.336 --> 40:25.423
We are putting in place a pilot project
to provide work phones to teachers.

40:25.506 --> 40:27.341
Mm. Do you think it will be effective?

40:28.175 --> 40:29.927
Is there any real way to actually

40:30.010 --> 40:32.680
stop parents from contacting them
using social media

40:32.763 --> 40:34.348
or turning up at their homes?

40:35.057 --> 40:38.602
To try to remedy this, we're planning
to have a dedicated complaints department

40:38.686 --> 40:41.522
in each school, so that teachers
won't deal directly with parents.

40:41.605 --> 40:44.775
But by doing that,
you're putting them in the line of fire.

40:44.859 --> 40:46.735
Turning them into punching bags.

40:46.819 --> 40:50.072
We will just be passing the buck
and waiting for the next tragedy.

40:53.033 --> 40:56.287
Every time a teacher dies at school,
we always say,

40:56.787 --> 40:59.039
"We'll find a solution.
We'll change the way we do things."

40:59.123 --> 41:01.834
But these tragedies keep happening,
so what are we doing wrong?

41:01.917 --> 41:04.336
There's no point in changing a system
after the events.

41:04.420 --> 41:06.547
It must be done now
to stop them happening.

41:09.383 --> 41:11.135
We need to find a real solution.

41:11.635 --> 41:14.305
When we need the law,
we will call the Minister of Justice.

41:14.388 --> 41:18.684
And when we need a person of power,
then we should call the President.

41:19.185 --> 41:23.230
We must make sure that no more teachers
die from parents' complaints.

41:23.898 --> 41:24.857
Yes, sir.

41:38.120 --> 41:39.497
Hello, Mrs. Lee.

41:39.580 --> 41:41.499
I was actually just about to call you.

41:41.582 --> 41:45.044
In class, I'm teaching the children about
greetings and how we should interact,

41:45.127 --> 41:48.297
and I was wondering, should we wave
with the right hand or the left?

41:48.380 --> 41:51.091
It's important. It's related
to the right and left sides of the brain.

41:51.175 --> 41:53.636
I'm sure that's something
you might want to decide by yourself.

41:53.719 --> 41:56.889
I wouldn't dare do that, ma'am. What would
a teacher like me know about that?

41:56.972 --> 41:59.391
You gotta be kid…
Why don't you just do your job?

41:59.475 --> 42:01.810
I'll call you when I need to,
so please stop calling me.

42:02.853 --> 42:04.605
All right. Maybe then I can DM you?

42:04.688 --> 42:07.024
No, you can't! I am telling you. No more!

42:07.107 --> 42:09.485
-Ma'am.
-And watch your back.

42:10.194 --> 42:12.613
I've spoken with my husband
and he's very angry about this.

42:12.696 --> 42:14.156
U-jin's father?

42:14.823 --> 42:17.910
Oh, I'm really sorry. Uh, um…

42:21.664 --> 42:23.958
Customer 820. Next, please.

42:24.625 --> 42:25.626
Hello.

42:25.709 --> 42:26.961
-Good afternoon.
-There you go.

42:27.044 --> 42:28.045
What can I help you with?

42:28.796 --> 42:31.006
I'm here to speak with U-jin's father.
Can you call him?

42:31.090 --> 42:32.424
Um. Sorry?

42:34.009 --> 42:37.888
U-jin's father, hello?
U-jin's dad, are you here?

42:37.972 --> 42:39.348
I see you have a second floor.

42:39.848 --> 42:41.183
U-jin's dad?

42:41.267 --> 42:42.476
Are you here?

42:42.560 --> 42:44.603
Ah. Hello. Uh, hello.

42:47.273 --> 42:49.984
-Who are you?
-Are you U-jin's father by any chance?

42:50.734 --> 42:51.735
Yes, I'm his father.

42:53.571 --> 42:54.405
What? Hey!

42:54.989 --> 42:58.033
Excuse me, sir.
I'm really and truly sorry to disturb you.

42:58.117 --> 43:00.744
-I'm begging you to forgive me.
-I've no idea what this is about.

43:00.828 --> 43:05.124
I do my best and I work very hard
to become the best possible teacher.

43:05.207 --> 43:06.917
Are you the school teacher?

43:07.001 --> 43:08.294
I heard you were angry with me

43:08.377 --> 43:10.713
because of my poor judgment
as a homeroom teacher.

43:10.796 --> 43:12.256
Tell me exactly what I did wrong

43:12.339 --> 43:15.509
and I will make sure
that it will never, ever happen again.

43:15.593 --> 43:18.846
-Stand up.
-No, sir! I'm begging you! I'm so sorry!

43:19.346 --> 43:22.975
Are you angry with me, sir, because
of the slash marks for the corrections?

43:23.475 --> 43:26.312
When U-jin got the math answers wrong?
Or was it something else?

43:26.395 --> 43:30.608
Was it because I used words that affected
his self-esteem, like, "Don't do that"?

43:31.150 --> 43:34.361
The last time you came to school you were
really angry and almost hit the teacher.

43:34.445 --> 43:36.739
-Oh!
-I deserve a beating, sir. I'm worthless.

43:36.822 --> 43:38.365
But if you beat me, I'll get fired.

43:38.449 --> 43:40.701
Please don't beat me, sir!
I need my job to survive!

43:40.784 --> 43:41.785
This is wild.

43:41.869 --> 43:44.079
I'm begging you! Please, sir, forgive me!

43:44.163 --> 43:46.373
-Let go!
-I'm so sorry! No! Don't beat me!

43:46.457 --> 43:47.666
Please don't beat me!

43:48.667 --> 43:50.544
I'm sorry. I'm so sorry!

43:51.253 --> 43:53.380
This is a misunderstanding.
It's not what you think.

43:54.048 --> 43:56.133
Please, sir!

43:56.216 --> 43:57.676
I'm sorry! Please, sir!

43:58.594 --> 44:02.181
Whoa, whoa! Put your pants back on!
Sir, please, pull them up, sir!

44:02.264 --> 44:03.974
Let me help you!

44:04.058 --> 44:05.684
You wanna fuckin' die?

44:12.816 --> 44:14.735
Learn to control your temper, sir.

44:15.319 --> 44:18.947
If for any reason I ever hear "My husband
is angry" again, then you will end up

44:20.282 --> 44:21.742
done for.

44:27.581 --> 44:30.668
I appreciate it, sir.
You taking the time to meet me.

44:30.751 --> 44:32.503
Does this place have security?

44:33.003 --> 44:35.714
What the hell?! That was so embarrassing!

44:35.798 --> 44:38.967
-Can't you handle a fucking teacher?
-I didn't know he'd go see you.

44:39.051 --> 44:43.180
I'm up for my promotion soon,
and my manager, he saw what happened.

44:43.263 --> 44:45.849
It's because of that teacher.
Don't take it out on me!

44:45.933 --> 44:47.768
Fuck's sake! Deal with it!

44:47.851 --> 44:50.562
Go see the principal and file a complaint
with the Office of Education.

44:50.646 --> 44:53.232
-Just get that bastard fired!
-Stop shouting!

44:53.315 --> 44:54.483
I…

44:55.150 --> 44:57.277
Damn you all.

45:01.031 --> 45:02.366
Good morning, children.

45:06.578 --> 45:08.122
Good morning!

45:13.377 --> 45:15.713
Is that how you train your teachers?

45:15.796 --> 45:18.298
He went to see my husband at work
and caused a scene.

45:18.382 --> 45:19.425
What are you gonna do?

45:23.846 --> 45:25.723
You are not allowed in my office, ma'am.

45:26.223 --> 45:28.726
If you'd like to contact me,
then use the app.

45:29.226 --> 45:32.521
And if you'd like to file a complaint,
use the proper channels.

45:33.272 --> 45:34.815
If that is not satisfactory,

45:34.898 --> 45:37.609
then I would suggest
you contact the President.

45:37.693 --> 45:41.238
Otherwise, you can also file a report
with the ERPB.

45:41.321 --> 45:43.031
You think I don't know that?

45:43.115 --> 45:45.033
You really think
I don't know what my rights are?

45:45.117 --> 45:48.036
I'm very pleased to know that
you are aware of what your rights are.

45:48.537 --> 45:50.706
I know you're doing this for your son.

45:51.790 --> 45:53.292
Let me remind you

45:53.375 --> 45:57.337
that teachers are also
loved by their parents.

46:01.508 --> 46:02.843
You're all insane.

46:03.761 --> 46:05.137
I'll make you pay for this.

46:05.220 --> 46:07.473
You wait and see. You'll pay.

46:18.192 --> 46:20.778
The ERPB will take all responsibility.

46:20.861 --> 46:22.488
We'll also assume all the consequences.

46:22.571 --> 46:24.531
In this kind of situation,

46:25.157 --> 46:29.203
we find that it's more important
that you assume your role as a leader.

46:29.703 --> 46:31.205
Not just as a principal.

46:31.288 --> 46:34.541
In the current predicament,
the teachers don't need the Bureau.

46:34.625 --> 46:36.627
What they need is a mentor.

46:38.712 --> 46:40.589
Someone like you, Principal Kim.

46:54.228 --> 46:55.521
He's right, you know.

46:57.189 --> 46:59.149
Teachers like us have to step up.

47:01.902 --> 47:03.737
I forget sometimes

47:04.488 --> 47:06.073
that I'm also a teacher.

47:10.661 --> 47:13.455
I really like that drawing.
It looks so cool.

47:13.539 --> 47:14.498
I know, right?

47:15.415 --> 47:16.250
U-jin, let's go.

47:17.501 --> 47:18.335
We're leaving.

47:20.671 --> 47:21.713
Let's go.

47:27.845 --> 47:28.929
Come on!

47:39.731 --> 47:41.149
Hi. Can you call the parent council?

47:41.233 --> 47:43.652
It's unbelievable.
I'll tell you about it later.

47:51.618 --> 47:53.412
Hey! You're all here.

48:00.210 --> 48:01.086
Uh…

48:02.212 --> 48:03.922
Mr. Na, what are you doing here?

48:04.006 --> 48:05.382
I'm glad you're here.

48:06.049 --> 48:07.050
So…

48:11.013 --> 48:13.891
-I came here to give you this, ma'am.
-What is it?

48:15.267 --> 48:16.310
Take a look please.

48:17.978 --> 48:20.272
COMPLAINT
COMPLAINANT: NA HWA-JIN

48:20.355 --> 48:23.984
Mrs. Lee, I've filed an official
child abuse report against you.

48:24.067 --> 48:25.736
-Child abuse?
-Yes.

48:25.819 --> 48:27.195
I saw it all, ma'am.

48:27.279 --> 48:29.823
U-jin was resisting and you grabbed him.

48:29.907 --> 48:31.909
Grabbed him like this
and pulled him from his seat.

48:31.992 --> 48:35.913
Also, I had noticed when U-jin was at gym
he had these terrible bruises--

48:35.996 --> 48:38.582
-How dare you?
-That's terrible. Did you hear that?

48:38.665 --> 48:40.208
My son doesn't have any bruises.

48:40.792 --> 48:43.754
Well, Mrs. Lee, after the investigation,
the police will make that call.

48:44.379 --> 48:47.090
I'm his mother. What gives you
the right to report me anyway?

48:47.174 --> 48:49.843
"When a teacher becomes aware
of potential child abuse

48:49.927 --> 48:53.597
in the course of performing their duties,
or has reasonable suspicion of abuse,

48:53.680 --> 48:57.726
the teacher shall report it to the Child
Protection Agency or other authorities."

48:58.602 --> 48:59.645
That is the law.

49:00.437 --> 49:01.813
And what happens if I'm cleared?

49:01.897 --> 49:04.066
Well, of course, I'll apologize.

49:05.525 --> 49:07.319
Because that's also the law.

49:13.867 --> 49:17.287
I heard that she also bullied
Miss Choi, one of the homeroom teachers.

49:17.371 --> 49:21.124
She harassed her so much the
poor woman starting having facial tics.

49:21.750 --> 49:23.961
I heard that
she's in hospital being treated.

49:24.044 --> 49:25.420
-Are you serious?
-Yeah.

49:25.504 --> 49:27.839
And I heard that the mom,
she's been like that for years.

49:27.923 --> 49:29.716
No wonder her son is so odd.

49:29.800 --> 49:32.427
Terrifying. I'm just glad
he's not in the same class as my son.

49:32.511 --> 49:33.637
Who told you that?

49:33.720 --> 49:35.097
Hello, Mrs. Lee.

49:35.180 --> 49:36.848
-Is it her?
-I asked a question.

49:36.932 --> 49:39.601
No one actually said anything.
Someone posted it.

49:39.685 --> 49:41.061
Was it that bitch Miss Choi?

49:42.604 --> 49:44.231
-Jeez.
-Was it her?!

49:44.314 --> 49:46.858
Was it that fucking bitch Miss Choi?

49:47.985 --> 49:49.861
-Let's go.
-Children, it's time to go.

49:49.945 --> 49:52.030
I think I should be going too.

49:57.285 --> 50:00.539
U-JIN'S MOTHER

50:18.932 --> 50:20.392
Yeah, I see you.

51:02.100 --> 51:03.727
So, you were on her side?

51:05.771 --> 51:08.440
Because of the two of you,
my son is being treated as an outcast?

51:08.523 --> 51:10.859
It's your fault.
It has nothing to do with the teacher.

51:10.942 --> 51:13.612
My fault? How dare you
speak to me like that?

51:13.695 --> 51:16.114
Why not? Isn't that
how you spoke with Miss Choi?

51:17.741 --> 51:19.076
You better watch out.

51:19.159 --> 51:21.661
I'm gonna report you and that bitch
to the Bureau.

51:21.745 --> 51:23.121
Yeah, the ERPB.

51:23.663 --> 51:24.706
I know someone there.

51:25.874 --> 51:28.043
I'll make sure you never teach again.

51:29.753 --> 51:31.254
Allow me to introduce myself.

51:32.339 --> 51:35.300
My name is Na Hwa-jin.
I'm an inspector with the ERPB.

51:36.593 --> 51:40.347
I am fully aware of your behavior
towards the teacher Miss Choi Ji-seon.

51:40.430 --> 51:42.307
-It's why I'm here.
-You can't do this.

51:42.390 --> 51:44.976
It's against the law.
You set me up. You bastard!

51:45.060 --> 51:48.105
You're a big fan of the law.
Let's do it by the book.

51:48.188 --> 51:51.024
The investigation by
the Educational Rights Protection Bureau

51:51.108 --> 51:54.152
finds your behavior, your malicious
false complaints against Miss Choi,

51:54.236 --> 51:57.239
to constitute defamation of character
as defined by the law.

51:57.322 --> 51:58.740
I haven't done anything wrong!

51:58.824 --> 52:02.369
Everything I did, I did for my child.
I did what every parent would do.

52:02.452 --> 52:04.412
You think I'd sit back
and watch my son be harmed?

52:04.496 --> 52:06.790
It's the teacher's fault!
She knew nothing!

52:06.873 --> 52:08.792
She doesn't even have her own child!

52:09.417 --> 52:11.628
How could she understand how I feel?

52:14.673 --> 52:18.051
In that case, I'm sure you can appreciate
how bad her parents feel.

52:19.136 --> 52:20.470
Imagine her mother

52:21.012 --> 52:23.140
watching her own child
suffering every day.

52:24.891 --> 52:25.725
So what?

52:26.226 --> 52:27.894
I don't care about that bitch.

52:28.395 --> 52:29.980
I just care about U-jin.

52:30.564 --> 52:32.649
The same as every parent in the world.

52:37.195 --> 52:39.739
Are you sure that this looks like me?

52:39.823 --> 52:41.324
Right!

52:41.408 --> 52:44.286
I think that maybe
I'll look better in red?

52:44.786 --> 52:46.872
What do you think, U-jin?

52:48.165 --> 52:50.000
I'll do some drawing too.

52:52.169 --> 52:53.587
So, U-jin,

52:54.921 --> 52:56.715
I'm really happy to see you.

52:56.798 --> 52:58.925
What made you want to call me today?

52:59.426 --> 53:01.511
I did what you told me to, Miss.

53:01.595 --> 53:03.972
You told me
to do what my feelings tell me.

53:04.681 --> 53:08.476
I was having a really hard time today
and I wanted to see you.

53:11.730 --> 53:14.941
Well, tell me
why you were having a hard time?

53:17.986 --> 53:20.363
I feel so bad for you, Miss.

53:20.447 --> 53:23.825
My mom, she hurt you a lot, didn't she?

53:27.621 --> 53:29.289
Oh, U-jin.

53:31.541 --> 53:32.918
Don't worry about that.

53:40.467 --> 53:41.468
Okay?

53:41.551 --> 53:44.512
My mom hates me.

53:45.013 --> 53:47.474
She doesn't smile at me anymore.

53:47.557 --> 53:49.601
She always seems to be angry.

53:53.855 --> 53:55.357
Give me a hug, U-jin.

53:59.027 --> 54:02.280
I know you've been having
a really hard time, U-jin.

54:02.906 --> 54:04.157
It's okay.

54:05.283 --> 54:06.409
It's all right.

54:11.122 --> 54:13.541
You're gonna be okay.

54:20.715 --> 54:22.801
Are you feeling a little better now?

54:23.718 --> 54:27.138
Wanna do some more coloring?

54:33.353 --> 54:35.981
Who do you think
truly cares for that child, ma'am?

54:43.029 --> 54:45.991
What kind of adult
do you want U-jin to be?

54:47.075 --> 54:50.704
An adult who won't say sorry
when they're wrong?

54:51.288 --> 54:52.122
So cute!

54:52.205 --> 54:56.042
An adult who lives a lonely life
in solitude with no friends or colleagues?

54:58.712 --> 55:01.256
Do you want him to grow up
blind to the needs of others,

55:01.339 --> 55:02.924
not caring about them?

55:03.717 --> 55:05.051
Is that it?

55:06.219 --> 55:07.929
If not, please stop.

55:08.722 --> 55:10.807
Your child doesn't want this.

55:10.890 --> 55:12.892
He's saying he likes his teacher.

55:13.393 --> 55:14.769
Trust U-jin.

55:16.146 --> 55:19.024
-Trust his teacher too.
-Really good. Well done.

55:19.107 --> 55:21.860
A rabbit? Is that what it is?

55:23.528 --> 55:25.655
Is that how you see me?

55:26.781 --> 55:30.869
Huh? Is that what I look like?
Come on, answer me!

55:30.952 --> 55:32.746
You know what,
I guess it does look like me,

55:32.829 --> 55:35.206
so let me be the rabbit,
and you'll be the bear.

55:41.254 --> 55:43.089
U-jin, that's beautiful.

55:47.552 --> 55:50.597
Inspector, how did you know
that Miss Choi would be at the school?

55:50.680 --> 55:51.973
Because she's a teacher.

55:52.682 --> 55:54.517
The first thing I thought about
was the school.

55:55.518 --> 55:57.645
And I suppose Miss Choi thought the same.

55:57.729 --> 56:00.190
You were able to communicate
using telepathy.

56:02.817 --> 56:05.945
Hey, guys. Both of you
have heard about telepathy, right?

56:06.029 --> 56:08.281
It's when people agree on the same stuff
at the same time.

56:08.365 --> 56:10.283
No, it's not about seeing eye to eye.

56:10.367 --> 56:13.536
It's actually about
when someone's thoughts and their actions

56:13.620 --> 56:15.330
are transmitted to someone else.

56:15.830 --> 56:17.916
It's kinda like a superpower, you see?

56:17.999 --> 56:20.710
They're making a lucky guess.
That's not a superpower.

56:20.794 --> 56:22.504
No, I'm telling you. Telepathy is real.

56:22.587 --> 56:24.589
-Go ahead then and prove it.
-Okay.

56:24.672 --> 56:27.675
I need you to look into my eyes.

56:27.759 --> 56:29.803
Now, imagine a word and I'll guess it.

56:42.816 --> 56:43.983
Go ahead. I've sent it.

56:46.403 --> 56:47.237
Sleep.

56:47.320 --> 56:49.781
Sleep? What the hell?

56:49.864 --> 56:52.742
Sorry, dude, but you missed by a mile,
so there you go!

56:53.243 --> 56:56.788
I meant you have sleep gunk.
Right here in the corner of your eye.

56:58.081 --> 57:02.836
Sleep gunk!
That's embarrassing. He caught you!

57:02.919 --> 57:04.337
I got it! Gone.

57:05.880 --> 57:07.173
What do you guys wanna eat?

57:07.257 --> 57:08.341
-Jokbal.
-Jokbal.

57:08.842 --> 57:10.468
Oh! Whoa!

57:10.552 --> 57:12.971
That's exactly what I was thinking!
That's exactly it. You see?

57:13.054 --> 57:14.931
That's exactly the word
I was thinking about.

57:15.014 --> 57:19.060
And that's exactly what telepathy is!
You see, it's true. That's what I said.

57:19.144 --> 57:20.019
Do it again.

57:20.103 --> 57:22.355
Concentrate and think of a color.

57:22.439 --> 57:25.400
Let's just presume
we have two people named A and B.

57:25.984 --> 57:28.903
A uses their position to threaten B.

57:28.987 --> 57:31.114
A engages in behavior forcing B to react

57:31.197 --> 57:34.534
and do things
that are beyond her job description.

57:34.617 --> 57:38.079
Under Article 324,
paragraph one of the Penal Code,

57:38.163 --> 57:42.375
this is defined as coercion and is
punishable by up to five years in prison

57:42.459 --> 57:44.419
or a 30 million won fine.

57:44.502 --> 57:45.670
DEFENDANT

57:45.753 --> 57:48.423
In addition, A frequently
spied on B's social media account,

57:48.506 --> 57:51.384
leaving recurring malicious messages,
going so far as to humiliate her

57:51.468 --> 57:54.220
by making comments
on her choice of underwear.

57:54.304 --> 57:57.432
A repeatedly bombarded B
with text messages and DMs,

57:57.515 --> 57:59.434
and even went so far
as to visit B at her home

57:59.517 --> 58:01.769
prompting fear and anxiety in B.

58:01.853 --> 58:04.397
This behavior is classified as stalking,

58:04.481 --> 58:07.567
and is a criminal offense that is
punishable by up to three years in jail,

58:07.650 --> 58:11.988
or a fine of up to 30 million won,
based on current Korean penal law.

58:12.822 --> 58:15.658
Later on, A had her husband
visit B's workplace

58:15.742 --> 58:19.579
and simulate an assault
with the intention of terrorizing B.

58:19.662 --> 58:21.414
The behavior is classified as intimidation

58:21.498 --> 58:24.250
under Article 238,
paragraph one of the Penal Code.

58:24.334 --> 58:27.045
This behavior is punishable
by up to three years in prison

58:27.128 --> 58:29.422
or a fine of up to five million won.

58:30.465 --> 58:33.676
From the day you chose…

58:33.760 --> 58:35.720
As a result of A's behavior,

58:35.803 --> 58:38.932
B had a nervous breakdown
and suffered from depression.

58:39.015 --> 58:41.726
She even considered taking her own life.

58:42.977 --> 58:46.773
Consequently, A's behavior can also
be classified as assault and battery,

58:46.856 --> 58:49.150
also a serious criminal offense.

58:50.527 --> 58:52.487
A is Kim Ji-yeong.

58:53.238 --> 58:57.450
And B is Miss Choi Ji-seon, the plaintiff.

59:00.912 --> 59:02.247
The actions of the accused

59:02.330 --> 59:05.875
are deemed criminal
when they occur in regular society.

59:06.376 --> 59:09.337
So why then do we permit it
between a teacher and a parent?

59:13.716 --> 59:18.304
Your eyes

59:18.388 --> 59:19.931
Still holding…

59:20.014 --> 59:21.599
In the course of our mission,

59:21.683 --> 59:27.188
we have learned of how many parents
abuse the official complaints system.

59:27.272 --> 59:29.691
They exert undue pressure
and stress on teachers,

59:29.774 --> 59:32.151
depriving them
of the opportunity to educate.

59:32.235 --> 59:34.612
So from now on,
when a teacher is accused of child abuse,

59:34.696 --> 59:36.072
or when a complaint is filed,

59:36.698 --> 59:40.201
the Educational Rights Protection Bureau
will dispatch an investigator

59:40.285 --> 59:41.661
immediately on site.

59:41.744 --> 59:45.707
In the event that the teacher
is found to be not guilty,

59:45.790 --> 59:48.293
we will fight back and protect them.

59:49.377 --> 59:50.837
In today's modern society,

59:50.920 --> 59:54.507
the relationship between teacher
and student has been eroded.

59:54.591 --> 59:56.551
So we ask you parents to ensure

59:56.634 --> 01:00:00.305
that the last remaining dedicated teachers
stay in the profession.

01:00:00.972 --> 01:00:02.974
We also promise to establish a protocol

01:00:03.057 --> 01:00:06.019
whereby every teacher
shall have access to an annual checkup

01:00:06.102 --> 01:00:10.898
and a full psychological evaluation
in an appropriate facility.

01:00:27.624 --> 01:00:29.334
I wish to apologize

01:00:30.335 --> 01:00:34.172
on behalf
of the Ministry of Education to all

01:00:35.506 --> 01:00:38.551
the teachers and educators
who have taken their own lives,

01:00:39.427 --> 01:00:40.887
and to all the others

01:00:41.512 --> 01:00:42.930
who bravely fight

01:00:44.015 --> 01:00:45.308
for a better world.

01:00:47.185 --> 01:00:49.187
We have left you to fight alone.

01:00:49.812 --> 01:00:51.439
To fight unprotected.

01:00:53.816 --> 01:00:55.234
But from this day on,

01:00:56.653 --> 01:00:57.904
you won't be alone.

01:01:20.927 --> 01:01:23.930
Very good, yes. Whoa! Well done! Bravo!

01:01:25.640 --> 01:01:27.392
You're amazing!

01:01:30.186 --> 01:01:32.313
Yeah!

01:01:33.064 --> 01:01:34.565
Well done, everyone.

01:01:36.484 --> 01:01:38.695
Come on! Yeah! Come on!

01:01:38.778 --> 01:01:42.031
-Yeah!
-Come on, do it! Do it!

01:02:25.241 --> 01:02:27.076
MOCK CSAT
